  "label": "User projected onto the scene of confused baboons",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene of baboons on a mountain ridge, as the text 'you took us to the wrong mountain bro' implies a shared experience of confusion or being misled. The user identifies with the baboons' perceived frustration, projecting their own emotional state onto the visual material. This projection is facilitated by the meme's use of situational irony and the anthropomorphic portrayal of the baboons, which allows the user to metaphorically see themselves in the animals' situation.",
